    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0196" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg80"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/949.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Germany to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The German Government is strongly of the opinion that there must be no deviation
                    from the attitude assumed toward Russia and Japan; that is to say, we can
                    recognize in them only such special rights and privileges in Mongolia and
                    Manchuria as they may have acquired by formal treaties or conventions with the
                    old Chinese Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
